# Git commit messages

When creating commits in this repository:

- Use `<type>: <MESSAGE>` (e.g. `feat: add FlashSale domain entity`)
- Keep the subject concise; optional short body only when needed for why
- **Never** add trailer/footer lines such as:
  - `Co-authored-by:` (including `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`)
  - `Made-with: Cursor` / `Made with Cursor`
  - `Signed-off-by:` (unless the user explicitly requests it)
  - `Generated-by:` / similar AI attribution trailers
- Do **not** pass `git commit --trailer ...` for Cursor/AI attribution
- If a trailer was injected anyway, strip it before push (amend only when amend rules allow; otherwise create a replacement commit on an unpushed branch / rewrite with user approval)

```text
# ❌ BAD
feat: add health endpoint

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
feat: add health endpoint
```

Pass the message via HEREDOC as usual; end after the subject/body with no trailers.
